<title>USA: Triarc sees $1 bln yrly bevs/restarant sales.</title>
<headline>Triarc sees $1 bln yrly bevs/restarant sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triarc Cos Inc said Monday it expects annualized sales of nearly $1 billion from its consumer brands in beverages and its Arby's restaurant chain.</p>
<p>Triarc, which sells the Snapple, Mistic and Royal Crown beverage brands, said it also expects annual sales of about $70 million in specialty dyes and chemicals from its C.H. Patrick unit's operations.</p>
<p>The company said it also has an equity interest in National Propane, a liquefied petroleum gas marketer, which has annual sales of about $175 million.</p>
</text>
